window.RRH_GUIDE_SEARCH_INDEX=[{"href":"index.html","title":"Home","text":"Round Robin Hood - User guide Version 0.9.3. Deutsch | Safety | Getting started RRH allocates measured solar export surplus to eligible consumers using configured power ratings, profiles and allocation strategies. Its control input is instantaneous grid power (W or kW), not a cumulative kWh meter. The grid reading already reflects power used by running appliances. Safety: This software can switch real equipment but cannot replace electrical or thermal protection. Errors can cause unexpected costs, overheating and damage. Read Safety before use. Chapters Installation and upgrades - backups and rollback. Setup - safety notice, wizard, demo and skip. Dashboard - measurements, actions, charts. Consumers - switches and adjustable appliances. Profiles and strategies - eight scheduling strategies. Conditions - thresholds and hysteresis. Energy and costs - tariffs, PV rating, estimates. Settings - operation, reserve, startup, demo and reset. Sensors - units, values and quality. Startup behavior - restoration after HA restart. Troubleshooting - problems and remedies. Safety , FAQ , Glossary , About . RRH has no metering hardware of its own and does not configure the Home Assistant Energy Dashboard. Nominal ratings and financial totals are estimates, not calibrated measurements."},{"href":"installation.html","title":"Installation & upgrades","text":"Installation, upgrades and rollback Fresh installation Create a restorable full Home Assistant backup including .storage . Copy custom_components/round_robin_hood from the package to /config/custom_components/round_robin_hood . Do not overwrite unrelated integrations. Restart Home Assistant Core, add Round Robin Hood under Settings > Devices & Services , then open its sidebar panel. Read the safety notice and choose the setup wizard, isolated demo or manual setup. Setup does not automatically activate loads. Upgrade an existing installation Use All OFF and physically verify that every configured actuator is off. Pause is not an electrical disconnect. Create a full Home Assistant backup including .storage and verify it can be restored. Follow the version-guarded upgrade in docs/UPDATE_0.9.3.md . This command is intended for v0.9.2 installations. Restart HA Core and verify existing consumers, profiles, sensors, statistics, startup behavior and All OFF . Rollback and recovery Restore the code and matching RRH data together . Never replace .storage while HA Core is running. RRH changes since the backup will be lost. Alternatively restore the verified full Home Assistant backup. RRH factory reset removes RRH data, not Home Assistant devices or recorder history. Back up first."},{"href":"setup.html","title":"Setup","text":"First-run setup and safety dialog Before the wizard On each fresh browser opening, RRH shows the safety notice until “Understood, do not show again” has been checked and saved. Clicking “Understood · continue” without checking only dismisses it for that view. Open it any time via Settings → Show safety notice . The preference belongs to the persistent real configuration, not the temporary demo. It does not constitute an electrical safety certification. Features and usage After acknowledging the existing safety notice, choose Start setup wizard , Try Demo mode or Skip setup . Demo uses a separate, temporary sandbox with six virtual consumers and never sends real HA switch commands. Skipping leaves RRH OFF and stores no grid source, consumer or profile. You can configure RRH manually or rerun the wizard from Settings. Factory reset returns to the safety notice and the same choices. “Do not show again” affects only the safety notice. Seven steps Introduction: Read the concept; setup will not start physical devices. Grid source: Select a sensor.* reporting instantaneous grid power (W/kW) and choose whether export is positive or negative . Do not select a cumulative kWh sensor. Stale readings prevent switching. Consumers: Add one or several existing switch.* entities, human-readable names and declared W . Every entity must be unique. Configure staged/variable devices later in the advanced consumer editor . Strategy: Choose one of eight strategies and read its explanation. Initial setup creates a default profile; reruns may alter the first profile's strategy. Energy & costs: Enter currency, optional PV nameplate watts, import tariff and feed-in tariff per kWh . Existing dynamic sources stay configured when their respective inputs are left blank. Controls: Set reserve watts, global deficit delay seconds, delay enable flag, and maximum sensor age. Summary: Review and save. Adding a real HA switch requires a separate explicit authorization confirming independent safety protection. RRH stays paused after saving; no new device is automatically turned on. Only start after safe-switch validation and a fresh correctly signed grid sensor. Restarting setup Open Settings → Restart setup wizard . Existing configurations require confirmation and Cancel never changes data. Existing consumers, other profiles, fairness counters and statistics are preserved. Be aware that rerunning can change the first profile's chosen strategy. Locale and initial defaults RRH first follows Home Assistant's language ( auto ; DE/EN for onboarding). Later select a manual UI language under Settings . Initial reserve is 100 W , global delay 30 s , maximum reading age 60 s ; adjust these to the actual installation."},{"href":"dashboard.html","title":"Dashboard","text":"Dashboard – every card and action Operation controls Indicator/action Meaning Operation Current controller state and any blocking reason. RRH ON Starts automatic allocation if configuration and fresh grid reading are valid; it may turn on real authorized devices. All OFF Requests OFF for RRH-managed devices; verify actual feedback. Not a certified physical emergency stop. Pause Suspends allocation; existing loads may stay running . Metrics and money Card Definition, unit and limitation Grid export Signed measured grid power in W; negative values mean import. Observe reading freshness. Additional available Positive export minus reserved watts, floored at 0 W. Total budget Additional available plus confirmed currently RRH-managed W; estimate, not a meter. Estimated managed power Sum of confirmed ON consumers' configured ratings in W. Net benefit now Estimated RRH-controlled kW × (purchase – feed-in tariff), currency per hour ; live rate, not cumulative. Missing tariffs show “—”. Accumulated net benefit Historical estimated credited energy value minus forgone feed-in income, not a guaranteed invoice saving. RRH-used surplus Estimated integrated RRH-attributed PV energy in kWh. Surplus utilization ratio Current managed load watts / reconstructed available positive surplus watts as a percentage; unavailable with invalid input. PV power Optional independent HA PV production sensor in W; installed nominal watts shown below where set. Full-width live chart The chart stretches over the full content row and offers gauge, line, bar, area, donut, stacked and sparkline . It depicts estimated capture percentage, not overall solar production. Hide/show any dashboard metric from Settings → Dashboard appearance & language . The chart stays full row when other cards are hidden. Current allocation order Profiles are shown in their priority order; member chips show physical state, planned watts, confirmed allocation, conditions and waiting reasons. Green marks confirmed RRH-owned ON consumers. Conditions may block an entire profile even with surplus. See Profiles and Energy & costs . Features and usage The dashboard now shows the international tagline Power your home. Not their profits. / Less to the grid. More for the little guy. The estimated live monetary benefit is displayed per hour with two decimal places; it is not a certified savings measurement. Estimated RRH-used surplus is also shown with two decimal places in kWh. The optional Buy me a drink link below lifetime net benefit opens an external donation page only when clicked; hide it under Settings → Dashboard . Control loop: If a rated 500 W device starts with 500 W net export and measured export consequently drops to 0 W, RRH must not stop it for that reason alone. Additional available power is the current positive export less reserve. Running owned watts are added only for estimated overall potential. Genuine import is handled by the configured deficit-shedding protections. Features and usage The optional donation link beneath Total net advantage now says “Buy me a drink” . Its information icon displays a hover/tap hint: “Large amounts of rum and cola fueled this project. That isn't free.” RRH embeds no third-party donation content until the external link is opened. Disable the link under Settings → Dashboard at any time."},{"href":"consumers.html","title":"Consumers","text":"Consumers – devices and safety limits Cards The responsive grid uses three equal-width slots on wide panels. With four or five devices, empty slots remain in the last row; narrow panels use two or one column. Each card shows name, MDI icon, confirmed state, planned/current watts, enabled flag, profile, waiting reason and relevant fairness credits. Action Result Participate / stop participating Allows/removes participation. An already running device may require controlled shutdown. ↑ / ↓ Reorders the global list; power-sorted strategies impose their own order. Edit Opens power mode, safety timers, icon and conditions. Remove Unassigns RRH, does not delete the HA entity . Unsafe removal of still-on owned devices is rejected. Basic editor fields Field Meaning / limit Name User label, 1–80 characters. Mode Switch , staged , continuously variable . Determines available HA actions. HA control entity Real entity, never shared between RRH loads. A new/rebound entity requires separate explicit authorization. Rated / minimum power (W) Positive, ≤100,000 W; scheduling estimate, not measured electricity. Participate Whether RRH can allocate this consumer; independent of HA state. Icon Clickable MDI gallery with preview, or PNG/WebP up to 48 KB; affects appearance only. Modes and extra fields Fixed switch ( switch.* ): single rated wattage, normal switch.turn_on/turn_off , feedback confirmation. Staged ( switch.* , select.* , climate.* ): stage-control entity, rows watts=option (e.g. 500=1 , 1000=2 ), an actual OFF option for select.* main controls. First stage is the minimum startup power. A climate fan mode is not proof of electrical wattage. Domain-specific OFF action is used. Variable ( number.* ): minimum and maximum watts , step resolution (W) , regulation hysteresis/minimum change (W) and minimum regulation interval (s) . The HA number must support actual 0 = OFF , report feedback and safely implement setpoints. Timing fields Field Effect Override shutdown delay Per-consumer 0–600 s, replaces global default. Minimum ON duration Hours/minutes/seconds during which voluntary rotation is deferred. Enforce minimum ON during shortfall May intentionally import grid electricity and incur costs; not a thermal safety mechanism. Restart cooldown Hours/minutes/seconds preventing rapid restart after OFF. Cooldown policy Skip blocked device or wait for it. Skip timer Overrides timing protection, with optional confirmation. Conditions and authorization Enable and combine individual sensor predicates using ALL or ANY . See Sensor conditions . Missing feedback or external commands must not be taken as successful RRH control. The old redundant editor checkbox was removed, but new or rebound real entity bindings still require explicit safety approval , and backend domain/action whitelists remain in place. Heaters require independent over-temperature and electrical protection. Features and usage The consumer editor no longer has a textual MDI dropdown. Choose an icon from the clickable preview gallery; the selected tile is highlighted. Existing saved icons survive an update. Custom PNG and WebP images remain supported."},{"href":"profiles.html","title":"Profiles & strategies","text":"Profiles, priorities and strategies A profile groups unique consumers; a consumer can belong to one profile only (except a separately assigned residual-surplus load). Profiles have ordered priority and, under safety constraints, a higher-priority profile may reclaim power from a lower one. Eight strategies Strategy Behavior Use case Classic Round Robin Rotate in fixed order; Strict or Skip when a load will not fit. Cyclic sharing. Fair Runtime Prioritize lowest confirmed RRH operating time; minimum gap/rotation delay limits thrashing. Balanced running hours. Fair Energy Prioritize least estimated credited Wh (declared W × runtime); uses a separate minimum credit gap. Consumers of differing wattage. Fixed Priority Highest listed eligible load first, Strict or Skip if insufficient power. Predictable priority. Maximum Efficiency Select a combination yielding greater surplus utilization; at most 24 consumers per profile. Maximize use of available watts. Power Ascending Prefer lower-watt loads; Strict or Skip. Favor smaller appliances. Power Descending Prefer larger-watt loads; Strict or Skip. Favor larger appliances. Stable Operation Favor continuity, avoid avoidable switching. Loads sensitive to repeated starts. Profile editor fields and defaults Field Meaning / default Name / enabled Unique display label and profile participation toggle. Priority ↑/↓ Profile order, separate from consumer ordering. Member list Unique consumer assignment across profiles. Strategy Allocation algorithm; relevant options nested inside one bordered group. Dashboard order Fixed or dynamic order where supported. Strict / Skip Strict can block later eligible loads when a candidate does not fit; Skip may proceed to a fitting one. Not available for every strategy. Fair comparison period Lifetime or fixed 24 h, 7 d, 14 d, 30 d. The wall-clock period does not stop during Pause. Fair rotation interval Minimum time between elective rotations, default 900 s (60–86400). Fair runtime gap Minimum credited time advantage, default 60 s . Fair energy gap Minimum credited energy advantage, default 10 Wh . Efficiency minimum gain Required extra watt usage, default 200 W . Optimization interval Minimum spacing between optimizations, default 60 s (10–3600). Efficiency start margin Extra safe startup headroom, default 50 W . Sensor conditions Profile-level ALL/ANY predicates and hysteresis. Reset fairness credit Resets selected fair score only; energy/money ledger and other score remain intact. Fair scores count only confirmed RRH allocation while the associated fair strategy is operating, not all lifetime appliance hours. Minimum-run, cooldown, data-quality rules and All OFF still apply. See Conditions . Profile participants The profile editor groups member selection and base order inside the labelled Profile participants fieldset. This is a presentation change; profile priority and strategy behaviour are unchanged."},{"href":"conditions.html","title":"Sensor conditions","text":"Sensor conditions – thresholds and hysteresis Conditions can be enabled per profile or per consumer . They block allocations when a numeric reading is missing or outside the selected threshold. A blocked profile prevents all member starts even if enough PV power is available. Field Meaning Sensor entity Existing numeric HA sensor.* (e.g. a room thermometer); unknown / unavailable are invalid. Comparison > , >= , < , <= . Threshold Numeric bound in the sensor's own unit. Hysteresis Return offset to avoid rapid state flapping. ALL Every predicate must pass. ANY One predicate is sufficient. Enabled If disabled, this condition group does not filter allocation. Example: allow a room heater only if sensor.room_temperature < 21 , with hysteresis 1 °C. A failed/missing sensor must not be treated as permission to start. This software rule is not an independent over-temperature cutout . Dashboard and cards show passed/total , invalid sensors and threshold details. Changing sensor/operator/threshold clears stale hysteresis latches. Read Safety ."},{"href":"energy.html","title":"Energy & costs","text":"Energy & costs – fields and calculations The page combines reporting with the single source for nominal PV size and tariffs. Save changes while RRH is paused . These entries influence estimates, not the physical reserve or Home Assistant's own Energy Dashboard. Configuration fields Field Meaning and unit Currency EUR , CHF , USD , GBP . Existing values are not exchange-rate converted . Check new local tariffs; existing valued history prevents currency changes until the ledger is explicitly reset. Nominal PV size (W) Fixed nameplate watts (e.g. 4000 ) or HA numeric entity; stored legacy kWp is displayed as watts ×1000. Informational, not a live power meter. Electricity purchase tariff (per kWh) Fixed or numeric HA entity, e.g. 0.30 EUR/kWh. Unitless helpers are not accepted as tariff sources. Feed-in remuneration (per kWh) What exported electricity would earn, e.g. 0.08 EUR/kWh. Higher export tariff than import price can make the net advantage negative. PV live power sensor Optional existing HA sensor.* with W/kW for displaying instantaneous production. PV cumulative energy meter Optional existing sensor.* with Wh/kWh/MWh for supplemental information. Grid export cumulative meter Optional energy meter; do not confuse it with the required instantaneous grid-power control source. Statistics cards RRH-captured energy (kWh): integrated, solar-attributed managed load; split between devices in proportion to confirmed nominal W. Potential surplus and remaining export (kWh): reconstructed only during valid live operation, never whole-system generation history. Gross value: credited kWh × purchase tariff. Foregone feed-in revenue: credited kWh × feed-in tariff. Net advantage: gross value less foregone feed-in income. Priced kWh: credited energy with valid tariff data; missing rates do not fabricate monetary values. Runtime, starts, per-consumer and daily totals: based on confirmed RRH states, separate from strategy fairness credits. Daily detail is bounded to 45 days, lifetime totals persist until manual reset. Real 24-hour history The chart depicts export utilization percentage for the last 24 hours on a real time axis. Formula: 100 × RRH-managed W / (RRH-managed W + positive measured export W) with valid fresh input. Y axis 0/50/100%; X axis hours before now. Typical interval 30 seconds, with at most 2890 stored history rows. Pauses, stale/missing data and outages create gaps , not interpolated usage. History is saved across HA restarts but no values are backfilled for the time before installation or while HA was stopped. It is not a utility-grade energy/money meter . Changing currency Priced EUR history cannot silently become CHF/USD/GBP. Export and explicitly reset the overall energy/statistics ledger first, then select a new currency and enter or explicitly reconfirm correct local purchase/feed-in tariffs. Check the unit of dynamic tariff sensors including cents/kWh and currency/MWh. Fairness credits are not reset alongside the energy ledger. Dashboard · Settings Features and usage Nominal PV capacity, import/feed-in tariffs, currency and optional HA sensors now appear above the statistics in a compact responsive three-column layout (two or one column on smaller screens). The section starts expanded. Existing values and sensor sources survive the update. Features and usage Sources are filtered by compatible units and currency; invalid live values are never priced. See Choosing sensors ."},{"href":"settings.html","title":"Settings","text":"Settings – every field and action Note: Editing affects the real controller; pause or turn all devices off and wait for in-flight commands. Pause does not necessarily turn devices off. Grid source Field Meaning / default Grid power source Existing sensor.* with instantaneous net W/kW, required for allocation. Sign Positive = export (default) or Negative = export ; choosing the wrong sign invalidates all available-watts decisions. Show data quality Visibility of the source freshness/diagnostics section, on by default. Power and switching Field Meaning / default Reserve W, default 100 , range 0–100,000; subtracts from positive export to reduce oscillation/grid import. Global deficit delay enabled On by default, delays normal shortfall OFF; All OFF remains immediate. Global deficit delay Seconds, default 30 , range 0–600; may temporarily draw from grid. Confirm skipping timers Request confirmation before manual override of minimum runtime/cooldown, on by default. Confirm disabling a profile Request confirmation for profile participation change, on by default. Residual-surplus consumer Optional one staged/variable load used last , never ahead of normal profiles. Data quality Field Meaning / default Maximum age of grid reading Seconds, default 60 , range 5–3600. Stale/unknown timestamps do not authorize new starts; a genuine new HA update can carry the same numeric value. Dashboard appearance and language Field Meaning Live chart type Gauge, line, bar, area, donut, stacked, sparkline; presentation only. Language auto follows HA locale; otherwise DE, EN, FR, ES, PT or IT. Some specialized feedback may fall back to English; all six UI languages are supported. Show/hide cards Grid, budget, managed power, live chart, live money, total money, used surplus, ratio, profile order and optional PV power. Full-width chart adapts if others are hidden. Tools Action Meaning Demo mode Completely separate in-memory scenario; entry requires the real controller fully OFF. Virtual loads, slider and synthetic stats never touch real HA services or financial ledger. Restart setup wizard Draft existing settings, save only after review; see Setup . Show safety notice Reopen warning at any time and optionally change persistence; see Safety . Reset overall statistics (Energy & costs page) Confirmed ledger reset, independent of fair-runtime/fair-energy credits. Old monetary totals are not re-labelled. Moved to Energy & costs: currency, PV nominal watts, tariffs and optional energy sensors are edited exclusively on Energy & costs . Features and usage Show donation link on dashboard: Shows/hides the optional Buy me a drink link; enabled by default for migrated installations. This does not change the energy ledger. Delete all RRH data: In Settings, open the factory-reset dialog and type exactly RESET ROUND ROBIN HOOD . RRH first dispatches All OFF , requiring confirmed OFF feedback from every configured actuator. Only then are RRH configuration, consumers, profiles, runtime/fairness history, statistics, setup flags and the stored safety acknowledgment cleared. No undo in RRH. Create a full HA backup including .storage first. If device confirmations or storage fail, check actual equipment and logs; do not blindly retry. External HA entities and recorder history are never deleted. After success, the safety notice appears before the first-use choice. Allocation does not start automatically. Features and usage Choose Always OFF (default), Always ON , or Restore last state . See Restart behavior for safety checks and physical-device caveats. Features and usage Settings cards now have equal heights within each grid row on wide displays, even when descriptions differ in length. The optional donation link reads “Buy me a drink” , with a tap- and hover-accessible information tip: “Large amounts of rum and cola fueled this project. That isn't free.” It is still configurable. First-time users can choose the wizard, a fully isolated Demo, or skip setup after seeing the safety notice."},{"href":"sensors.html","title":"Sensor types","text":"Choosing valid Home Assistant sensors RRH uses control inputs and statistics inputs for different purposes. The grid-power sensor provides the switching budget; prices and PV meters affect statistics only. What belongs where? Field Supported unit Use Grid power W or kW Actual export/import and dispatch decisions Nominal PV capacity W, Wp, kW or kWp Installed capacity; not current generation Actual PV power W or kW Current PV generation display PV energy counter Wh, kWh or MWh Extra cumulative statistics Import tariff Currency/kWh, EUR cents/kWh or currency/MWh Valuation of self-consumed energy Feed-in tariff Same as import tariff Opportunity cost of not exporting energy The source picker offers only compatible numeric sensor.* entities. An unlabelled 0.32 is ambiguous : for a new price source, use a Home Assistant template sensor with an explicit unit_of_measurement . Currency must match the selected RRH currency. Unavailable or invalid measurements Grid power : no new control action may be based on invalid or stale readings. Existing running loads are not physically disconnected merely because a reading failed. Prices/PV sources : invalid, unavailable or restored readings are omitted from financial calculations and surfaced as source warnings; RRH does not invent a fallback tariff. Price-sensor loss does not stop the PV surplus controller. Conversions ct/kWh ÷ 100 = EUR/kWh, EUR/MWh ÷ 1,000 = EUR/kWh, kW × 1,000 = W, Wh ÷ 1,000 = kWh. RRH measures the remaining export after its controlled consumers have drawn power. Do not subtract running loads a second time. See Dashboard . If a source is absent from the picker, check its unit, value, state and configured currency in Home Assistant Developer Tools. Incompatible previously saved sources stay visible with a warning; they are not silently replaced."},{"href":"startup.html","title":"Restart behavior","text":"Restart behavior Choose RRH → Settings → Behavior on Home Assistant restart . Option Behavior Always OFF (default) RRH does not resume its automatic controller after reboot. This is not a physical OFF command to devices that were already on. Always ON RRH attempts to start only after its safety checks have succeeded. Restore last state Previously running → attempt to start; paused → remain paused; OFF → remain stopped. Features and usage Always ON and Restore last = ON now work for manually configured installations even when the optional setup wizard was not completed. RRH stays paused while the automatic start is pending. It starts only after all configured HA actuators return a known on / off state and a new valid grid-power report arrives after HA restart. Late-appearing entities no longer cancel the startup intent permanently. Unresolved switching or a bad grid source still blocks automation. Device ON states are never blindly restored. Safety gate before any automatic dispatch Valid grid source, configured consumers and an enabled profile (wizard completion is optional). No pending or unresolved prior switching commands. All configured actuator states observed as on / off ; never blindly adopt an externally controlled load. A new valid grid report must arrive after restart; a cached reading cannot dispatch a command. Unavailable data keeps the controller paused with a diagnostic reason. Unresolved prior commands require manual action. Restart policy does not blindly restore physical switch states. Pause stops RRH decisions but does not turn running appliances off. For heaters or unattended electrical loads, prefer Always OFF and use independent safety hardware. RRH is not a certified emergency stop."},{"href":"troubleshooting.html","title":"Troubleshooting","text":"Troubleshooting and recovery RRH does not resume after restart Check Settings → Restart behavior, the configured power sensor (unit, sign and freshness), all configured actuator states and Home Assistant Core logs. The default policy is Always OFF. Unknown actuators and unresolved All OFF commands block automatic restart. A tariff sensor is missing from the picker Verify a numeric state and a currency-matching unit such as EUR/kWh or ct/kWh . Temperature, power, energy and unitless sensors must not be selected as tariff inputs. See Sensor types . No consumer starts Inspect export, reserve, enabled profiles, eligibility conditions, minimum runtimes, cooldowns, nominal watts, external state changes and confirmation errors. Pause does not disconnect power; All OFF requests and confirms off actions separately. Upgrade or storage problem Preserve a full Home Assistant backup including .storage and consult the matching docs/UPDATE_*.md for the exact upgrade/rollback procedure. Do not rerun a failed install blindly. RRH uses .storage/round_robin_hood.rebuild_2026.state for its own persistent state."},{"href":"safety.html","title":"Safety","text":"Safety and liability information Round Robin Hood is a private hobby project , initially built for its developer's personal use, with AI assistance in development and documentation. No damage-free operation or guaranteed savings are promised. It is not a certified safety controller or physical emergency stop . Mandatory statutory rights are not categorically waived by this notice. Main risks Bugs, incorrect measurements, integrations, network delays or device services can cause loads to run unexpectedly, stay on, start at the wrong level or shut down late . Heaters may overheat or start fires if installed near combustible material or operated without independent protection. Mains equipment also poses electric-shock risk. HA feedback does not prove actual physical safety. Poor threshold selection, strict runtime settings, or inaccurate ratings can cause unplanned grid imports, electricity bills and lost feed-in compensation . An HA/RRH/network/power failure can prevent a software OFF command from reaching the actual device. Software never replaces independent thermal cutouts, thermostats, breakers, residual-current protection, compliant installation or supervision . Required precautions Use appropriately rated and protected equipment, with competent electrical installation. Position heating appliances securely, away from flammables, in accordance with manufacturer instructions; never rely on software alone for unattended operation. Verify true power draw and actual OFF responses in a safe test setup. A number value of 0 must actually switch off; test every staged-level and OFF route. Check grid-meter sign, update timestamps and missing-sensor behavior. Use conservative reserve and delays. Before updates use All OFF , inspect real actuators and back up HA. Test updates in demo/isolated demo first. All OFF is a software command only. Maintain an independent physical disconnect for emergencies. Notice recurrence The notice reappears on opening until “Understood, do not show again” is deliberately checked and stored. The checkbox is not authorization for unattended devices. The dialog can be reopened under Settings at any time."},{"href":"faq.html","title":"FAQ","text":"FAQ and troubleshooting Why will no load start even though PV is generating? RRH uses the net grid-power sensor , not overall PV generation. Check export sign, freshness, reserve, state, conditions, nominal watts, cooldown and active profile. Pause versus All OFF? Pause suspends allocations and may leave loads on; All OFF requests OFF for RRH-managed loads. Independent physical disconnection is required for actual emergencies. Why is money shown as a dash? Import/feed-in tariff unavailable or invalid. RRH does not retroactively invent prices for previously unpriced kWh. Why is the 24h chart empty or discontinuous? Invalid readings, Pause, HA downtime/restart, stale values or less than 24 hours of collected history. The graph only shows observations RRH actually made. Why is currency switching rejected? Existing priced money history is protected from silent re-labelling. See Energy & costs for export, reset and correct local tariff entry. Why doesn't the setup wizard auto-run after an upgrade? Existing configurations are preserved. Only a truly empty install shows the automatic wizard; rerun it manually from Settings. Can I type an icon name? The free-text icon field was removed. Choose an icon from the clickable gallery instead; custom PNG/WebP images up to 48 KB are also supported. Can I pick any HA control? No. Only supported switch , select , climate and number actions are whitelisted. New bindings require explicit authorization. Why is a device off although surplus is available? Review profile assignment, conditions, reading freshness, strategy order, power margin, cooldown and fairness advantage. Cards explain common blocking reasons. Can I use existing HA Energy Dashboard sources? Yes, select suitable existing sensor entities; RRH neither configures the Energy Dashboard nor imports historical energy data. Why are some words in German? auto follows HA language. The KB is complete in DE/EN for this version; some legacy specialized UI messages may still fall back to DE/EN for FR/ES/PT/IT. How do I report a bug? Note version, page/action, sanitized HA logs, safe test setup, expected and actual results. If an actuator behaves dangerously, physically isolate it before troubleshooting."},{"href":"glossary.html","title":"Glossary","text":"Glossary Term Meaning PV Photovoltaic solar electricity generation. Grid export Instantaneous power sent to grid; sensor sign is configured. Grid import Instantaneous power purchased from grid. W Watt, instantaneous electrical power; enter a 4 kW nameplate as 4000 W. Wh / kWh Energy = power × time; 1000 W for one hour = 1 kWh. kWp Nameplate PV capacity under standard test conditions; RRH displays the system rating in W. Reserve Watts deliberately held back from allocations. Hysteresis Return gap preventing frequent toggling near a threshold. Allocation RRH-planned and confirmed usage of a consumer. Fairness credit Credited RRH runtime or estimated Wh, separate from general statistics. Strict / Skip Wait for blocked next candidate vs. consider a fitting one. Residual-surplus load Lowest-priority adjustable device using watts left after normal profiles."},{"href":"about.html","title":"About","text":"About Round Robin Hood Round Robin Hood (RRH) is a Home Assistant integration that allocates photovoltaic export surplus to configurable appliances. Satisfried (Satisfried_yt) originally created it for personal use, with the assistance of artificial intelligence. It supports allocation strategies, profiles, switches and adjustable consumers, sensor conditions, safety margins, an isolated demo, estimated energy/cost statistics, a setup wizard and integrated documentation. Important: RRH is not a certified safety controller, a physical disconnect or a calibrated energy meter. Read Safety before using it. Financial figures are estimates rather than guaranteed savings. Publisher Satisfried Satisfried_yt GitHub YouTube TikTok Twitch The About page shows the installed RRH version and the HA Core version when Home Assistant supplies it. Unavailable system versions are not guessed. Copyright (c) 2026 Satisfried. Round Robin Hood is licensed under Apache License 2.0. This does not grant trademark rights in its names or logos; see LICENSE and BRANDING.md in the project repository."}];
